---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { translations } from '../i18n/ui';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy - Stargazing Hub">
  <main class="legal-page mx-auto text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-8">Privacy Policy</h1>

    <div class="space-y-6">
      <p class="text-lg">Last updated: August 9, 2026</p>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">1. Scope</h2>
        <p>
          This policy explains how Stargazing Hub handles information when you visit
          stargazinghub.com or use the Stargazing Hub mobile app. The website and the
          app use different systems, so their data practices are described separately.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">2. Website analytics</h2>
        <p>
          On the official Stargazing Hub domain, we use Matomo to understand which
          pages people visit and which store links they choose. The browser tracker
          records page views, link activity, and a Download event containing the store
          name and the placement of the link. Analytics requests are sent to the
          configured Matomo endpoint at matomotech.com.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-3 space-y-2">
          <li>The tracker is configured without analytics cookies.</li>
          <li>It is configured to honor a browser's Do Not Track signal.</li>
          <li>It does not load on local development or preview domains.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          As with any web request, the analytics server receives technical connection
          data such as an IP address and browser user agent. We use website analytics
          to maintain the site, evaluate content, and measure store-link performance.
          The website does not ask you to create an account or submit location data or
          sky photos.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">3. Mobile app data</h2>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2">Location</h3>
        <p>
          With your permission, the app uses your location for on-device astronomical
          calculations and location-based weather, map, elevation, and geocoding
          features. Coordinates are sent to the relevant service providers when those
          online features are used. Selected and recent locations may be stored on
          your device. You can control location access in iOS or Android settings.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mt-5 mb-2">Sky photos</h3>
        <p>
          Eligible wide-field sky photos can be solved entirely on the device without
          upload. A photo is uploaded only when you choose Online Solve, including an
          online fallback offered after a local solve fails. Online solves use the
          Stargazing Hub astrometry service and may fall back to Astrometry.net. The
          request is marked as non-public. Depending on the image-processing path, an
          uploaded file may retain embedded metadata such as EXIF data. Recognition
          history and related image files may also be stored locally on your device.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mt-5 mb-2">App analytics and advertising</h3>
        <p>
          Subject to the app's privacy controls, the app uses Umeng Analytics for page
          usage, subscription-funnel, and technical reliability events. Free users may
          receive ads from Google AdMob or, in mainland China configurations,
          Pangle/GroMore and Tencent GDT. These providers may process app and device
          information, ad interactions, network information, and pseudonymous device
          or advertising identifiers. Google advertising uses its consent flow, and
          iOS advertising identifiers are subject to App Tracking Transparency where
          applicable. Advertising SDKs are not initialized for subscribers.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mt-5 mb-2">Identifiers, purchases, and accounts</h3>
        <p>
          The app and its service providers may use pseudonymous app, device, or
          advertising identifiers for API security, subscription management,
          analytics, and advertising. Some remote service requests include an app or
          device identifier for access control and abuse prevention.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Subscriptions are processed through Apple or Google. Google Play builds may
          use RevenueCat with an anonymous app user ID to manage entitlements. After an
          iOS purchase, renewal, or restore, the app may send a private operational
          sales notice through Feishu/Lark. That notice can include the product,
          transaction and expiry times, storefront country, currency and amount,
          purchase status, app version, and a locally generated device identifier.
          Stargazing Hub does not currently provide user registration or sign-in.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">4. Use, disclosure, and legal basis</h2>
        <p>
          We use information to provide requested features, keep the website and app
          working, understand performance, prevent abuse, and comply with legal
          obligations. We disclose information to service providers only where needed
          for those purposes, or when law requires it. We do not treat a third party's
          privacy policy as a substitute for our own responsibilities.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Our legal basis depends on the information, feature, and your location. It
          may include performing a service you requested, legitimate interests in
          operating and improving the service, consent, or compliance with law. Where
          applicable law requires consent for a particular activity, we will request
          it. You may withdraw consent at any time without affecting earlier lawful
          processing.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Service providers may process information outside the country where you
          live. When applicable law requires safeguards for an international transfer,
          we remain responsible for putting those safeguards in place.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">5. Retention and security</h2>
        <p>
          We keep information only for as long as needed for the purposes described in
          this policy, including security, dispute resolution, and legal requirements.
          Retention can vary by data type and service. We use reasonable technical and
          organizational measures to protect information, but no internet or storage
          system can be guaranteed completely secure.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">6. Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can control app permissions in your device settings and enable Do Not
          Track in a supported browser. Depending on where you live, you may also have
          rights to access, correct, delete, or receive your personal data, and to
          restrict or object to certain processing. You may have the right to complain
          to your local data protection authority. These rights are subject to the
          conditions and exceptions in applicable law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">7. Third-party links and services</h2>
        <p>
          The website and app link to or rely on third-party services, including app
          stores and data providers. Those providers may process information under
          their own privacy policies. We review the services we choose and remain
          responsible for our obligations when we use a provider to process data on
          our behalf.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">8. Contact us</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions or requests, email
          <a class="text-white underline underline-offset-4" href="mailto:support@stargazinghub.com">support@stargazinghub.com</a>.
          We may need to verify your identity before completing a request.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer t={translations.en} lang="en" />
</Layout>
